course: dictionary
lesson: 7922
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word first, then ask which meaning fits this sentence.
explain: The word react is a good example. «How did she react to the news?» means act or feel in a certain way. «Gold almost never reacts with oxygen or sulphur» means it does not change when it touches them. Same word, different job.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right one. If not, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: React means to act, speak or feel in a certain way because of something that has happened.
fact: In science, to react means to change when mixed with another substance, making something new.
fact: To react can also mean to become ill or get a rash after eating, touching or breathing something.
fact: The noun from react is reaction, as in «an allergic reaction».
fact: «React against» means to do the opposite of what you are told or what others do.
exercise: «How did she react to the news?» What does react mean here? | To change when mixed with another substance | To cook a meal | To become ill after eating something | *To act or feel in a certain way because of something that happened
exercise: In science, when vinegar and baking soda react, what do they make? | *Carbon dioxide gas, which fizzes | A new ring | Dust | A bright red rash
exercise: «Gold almost never reacts with oxygen or sulphur, so it does not tarnish.» What does reacts mean here? | To move quickly away | *To change chemically when it meets another substance | To cover in paint | To sing loudly
test: «Some people react badly to peanuts and need help fast.» What does react mean here? | *To become ill or get a rash after eating something | To act in a calm, careful way | To fall asleep | To change colour in the sun
test: Sam decided to react against what his friends told him to do. What does react against mean? | To run home | *To do the opposite of what he was told | To agree at once | To forget the plan
exam: Which sentence uses react in the sense of a chemical change? | Yesterday I reacted to a funny joke by laughing. | The bee sting made his arm react badly. | *In class, the lime water goes milky because carbon dioxide reacts with it. | She reacted quickly and caught the ball.
